      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While retraining is a valuable tool, it assumes a future labor market that continuously creates matching roles for displaced workers—a premise increasingly challenged by AI-driven obsolescence rates. Instead, UBI addresses the fundamental risk that a large portion of the workforce may never fully reintegrate due to the sheer scale and unpredictability of technological displacement. Consequently, UBI acts as an economic floor that provides stability and frees individuals to pursue entrepreneurial opportunities or new career paths beyond traditional retraining pipelines. For your article, highlighting the gap between current \"upskilling\" strategies and the non-linear nature of AI disruption could effectively demonstrate why a decoupling of income from employment is ultimately more robust.",
